## What to review

1. `poc/eval/gold/grouping-identity-gold-2026-10-25.json`: identity labels (same / part_of / related_not_same / different) and group memberships (required / optional / forbidden) across ledgers G (`poc/data/english-groups4-2026-10-25/views.sqlite`), E (`poc/data/english-2026-10-25/views.sqlite`), C (`poc/data/views-2026-10-25-v15-T4c.sqlite`), S (`poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite`). For every labelled pair and every required/forbidden member, read the thesis rows (`views`: looks_at, question; `view_keys`) and the initiating evidence (`evidence` joined through `evidence_links`, `evidence_sources`; source text in `poc/data/items-window-tags2-2026-10-24.sqlite` table `items`, column `text`, keyed by `input_id`) and say whether the label holds under the definitions in `docs/prd/06-views.md` (identity: section "Existing identity or part, succession, new thesis or skip"; research groups: the grouping contract) and `docs/DECISIONS.md` D149, D154, D165, D166. Name every label you would change, with the sentence of the source that decides it. Pay special attention to: the Chinese financing set C v17/v22/v24 (are they one quantity?), C v18/v21 (provisional), S v16/v48, G v1/v20 and E v11/v19 (related or part_of?), S v72/v89, the `_disputes` entries (Vera CPU as a Rubin-rollout member; company capex lines in the capex cycle vs D165), and the eleven C theses the gold leaves unlabelled for the Rubin, capex and China-controls matters (v1, v7, v8, v9, v11, v13, v14, v15, v16, v25, v39): what should each be?
