What Happened?
NVIDIA ( NVDA ) closed at $208.76 on July 23, up about 12% from its $186.27 close at the end of 2025, while AMD and Intel gained roughly 128% and 149% as of July 21. The two server CPU incumbents have led the chip group all year, which makes the timing of NVIDIA’s July 21 disclosure worth reading closely.
That day, one before AMD’s Advancing AI conference, NVIDIA published the full architecture and benchmarks for Vera, its first CPU built on custom Olympus cores. Shares rose 2.30% in a session where the broader chip tape also gained. The specs matter less than the revenue number management attached to them in May, and where that number does not appear.
