Nvidia ( NASDAQ:NVDA ) could face additional financial risk if it provides backing for a large OpenAI data center project in Ohio, although the arrangement may strengthen its long-term position in the artificial intelligence market, according to a research note from Wedbush.
The brokerage said reports of a potential $250 billion financial backstop would deepen Nvidia's relationship with one of the world's leading AI model developers. However, it cautioned that such financing could leave the chipmaker more exposed if AI demand weakens or OpenAI loses momentum against competing developers.
